  "claim": "The musical director of Jazz on a Summer's Day is also a producer. Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an Armenian professional wrestler, the producer and Bobby Managoff were not.",
  "evidencia": "Page: George Avakian. Sentence: George Avakian (Armenian: Գևորգ Ավագյան ; Russian: Геворк Авакян ; born March 15, 1919) is an American record producer and executive known particularly for his work with Columbia Records, and his production of albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis and other notable jazz musicians.\nPage: Bobby Managoff. Sentence: Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent who was best known for his work with National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s as Bobby Managoff.\nPage: Jazz on a Summer's Day. Sentence: The Columbia Records jazz producer, George Avakian, was the musical director of the film.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: George Avakian. Sentence: George Avakian (Armenian: Գևորգ Ավագյան ; Russian: Геворк Авакян ; born March 15, 1919) is an American record producer and executive known particularly for his work with Columbia Records, and his production of albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis and other notable jazz musicians.\nPage: Bobby Managoff. Sentence: Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent who was best known for his work with National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s as Bobby Managoff.\nPage: Jazz on a Summer's Day. Sentence: The Columbia Records jazz producer, George Avakian, was the musical director of the film.",
