        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Avakian, Bobby Managoff\n- Companies: Columbia Records, National Wrestling Alliance\n- Works: Jazz on a Summer's Day\n- Roles: record producer, executive, musical director, professional wrestler\n\nFacts:\n- George Avakian was born on March 15, 1919.\n- Bobby Managoff, born Robert Manoogian Jr., was born on January 4, 1918, and died on April 3, 2002.\n- George Avakian was an American record producer and executive known for his work with Columbia Records.\n- George Avakian produced albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis, and other notable jazz musicians.\n- George Avakian was the musical director of the film Jazz on a Summer's Day.\n- Bobby Managoff was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent best known for his work with the National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s.",
